          "**Likelihood ratios** are prevalence-independent: **LR+ = sensitivity / (1 - specificity)** and **LR- = (1 - sensitivity) / specificity**; LR+ over 10 or LR- under 0.1 changes probability decisively, while 0.5-2 is nearly useless. [Park 28e]",
          "**Post-test odds = pre-test odds x LR**, which is the bedside use of a likelihood ratio (Fagan nomogram). [Park 28e]",
