      "Health planning (WHO) is the orderly process of **defining community health problems, identifying unmet needs, surveying resources, setting realistic priority goals and projecting administrative action**; management gets the plan done **through and with people** (POSDCORB); the two run as an **eight-step planning cycle** that closes when evaluation feeds a fresh situation analysis, supported by **cost-effectiveness analysis, network analysis (PERT, CPM) and SWOT-TOWS**, and in India by **NHP 2017, NHM PIPs and NQAS**.",
